Add a Reset Section button to the configure dialog

The button sits under the section list and resets only the
section that the stack shows. It reads the same defaults source
as the Restore Defaults path, the (Default) preset. It applies
only the fields of the shown section over the live widget state.
The write reuses the setPreset() tail: one setWidgetOptions()
call over the merged options, the preview test, the changed(true)
test and the gradient list rebuild.

The Window Manager section resets through kwin->defaults() alone.
The Presets and Preview section and the Legacy section own no
option and keep the button disabled. The thin flags split by
page. The drop shadow size follows the live X11 value on this
tree, so the copied default cannot move that spin box.

The section field map lives once, in sectionmap.h.

Move the Reset Section button below the page area

In the sidebar, the button reads as a reset of the whole dialog.
It resets only the section that the stack shows.

A footer below the page stack now holds the button. The footer
holds a sunken line and then a row with the button at the left.
A spacer fills the rest of the row. The footer pins the button to
the page area, under the section that it resets.

The section list now also spans the footer row. The list runs the
full height of the page stack and the footer.

The button is now the last tab stop. Seventeen page controls had
no tab stop. They took focus after the controls with a tab stop.
Each of them now has a tab stop at its place in the page layout.

The dialog adds the Window Manager page at run time. The .ui file
cannot set the tab order of the controls on that page. A call now
puts the button after these controls. Focus goes from the section
list to the page controls and then to the button.

When another QtCurve configuration dialog is already open, the
dialog shows a note alone. It hides the title, the section list
and the button. It now hides the line as well.

The changes sit on the branch work/section-reset of the local tree, as
commits 1 and 5 of 6. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge
request !30 on system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

